<div tabindex="-1" role="dialog" class="ui-dialog ui-corner-all ui-widget ui-widget-content ui-front ui-draggable ui-resizable" aria-describedby="news-dialog" aria-labelledby="ui-id-1" style="position: absolute; height: auto; width: 600px; top: 147.5px; left: 464px; display: none;"><div class="ui-dialog-titlebar ui-corner-all ui-widget-header ui-helper-clearfix ui-draggable-handle"><span id="ui-id-1" class="ui-dialog-title">News</span><button type="button" class="ui-button ui-corner-all ui-widget ui-button-icon-only ui-dialog-titlebar-close" title="Close"><span class="ui-button-icon ui-icon ui-icon-closethick"></span><span class="ui-button-icon-space"> </span>Close</button></div><div class="all-dialogs ui-dialog-content ui-widget-content" id="news-dialog" style="width: auto; min-height: 0px; max-height: none; height: 346.8px;">
        <form id="news-dialog-form" onsubmit="return false;">
            <div id="newsitem"><p><b>November 4, 2025 - AI Tokens Increased to 100k!</b></p>
<p> UPDATE: We have increased the number of AI tokens to 100,000 for all subscriptions!</p>
<p>PlantText Pro is now live!</p>
<ul>
    <li>Enjoy an ad-free experience</li>
    <li>GitHub integration: Open diagrams from and save diagrams to GitHub</li>
    <li>Pro users get up to 100,000 AI tokens per week</li>
    <li>Convert diagrams to PDF as well</li>
    <li>Autocompletion and Snippets upgrades</li>
</ul>
<p>Discover more about Pro <a href="https://blog.planttext.com/pro/" target="_blank">here</a>.</p>
<p>Or click <a href="https://www.planttext.com/" target="_blank" onclick="openJqueryUiDialog(&#39;subscribe-dialog&#39;); return false;">here</a> to get started...
<span class="buttonbar-item" id="subscribe-link-div" title="PlantText Pro">
    <button class="basic-button" id="buttonbar-subscribe-button" onclick="openJqueryUiDialog(&#39;subscribe-dialog&#39;); return false;" type="button">
         <img alt="Subscribe" src="./s5_files/cart-2x(1).png">
    </button>
</span>
</p>
<p>New to PlantText? Here are the basics:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Add PlantUML, JSON, or YAML text into the editor and press Refresh to convert it into a diagram image.
    Open and share your diagram with the links below the diagram. </li>
    <li>The diagram text is compressed into the link URL. This makes it easy to share, but treat links like a document. Only 
    share links with people you want to have the full document text.</li>

    <li>The PNG, SVG, PDF, and TXT links create a diagram in that format. The "Share" link copies a link to
    your clipboard that opens a new PlantText window preloaded with the text copied into a new local file.</li>

    <li>All PlantText data, including diagram text, is stored in your browser's local storage. Use 
     the "Delete Local Data" button in Settings to remove all PlantText data from your browser. </li>
    <li><u>Do not use PlantText 
        if you do not consent to save cookies and data to local storage.</u> You can also use your browser-specific "Clear Browsing
    Data" feature to remove all PlantText data from your browser.
</li></ul>
<p>
</p><div style="float:left; margin: 5px;">
    <div title="News" class="buttonbar-item">
        <button type="button" class="basic-button" onclick="alert(&#39;You are already in the News window silly!&#39;)" style="vertical-align: middle;">
            <img src="./s5_files/bullhorn-2x(1).png" alt="Latest news">
        </button>
    </div>
</div>
You are currently viewing the News window. Clicking the News button in the right toolbar opens this window. When there is something noteworthy, you will see it here. 
<p></p>

<p>
</p><div style="float:left; margin: 5px;">
    <div title="Samples" class="buttonbar-item">
        <button type="button" class="basic-button" onclick="openJqueryUiDialog(&#39;samples-dialog&#39;); return false;" style="vertical-align: middle;">
            <img src="./s5_files/eye-2x(1).png" alt="Settings">
        </button>
    </div>
</div>
Click the Samples button to work with hundreds of plantuml diagrams. Select a category and then a specific diagram. Notice the PlantUML and resulting diagram appear below. Take a look and add it to the editor if you want to work with it.
<p></p>

<p>
</p><div style="float:left; margin: 5px;">
    <div title="Settings" class="buttonbar-item">
        <button type="button" class="basic-button" onclick="openJqueryUiDialog(&#39;settings-dialog&#39;); return false;" style="vertical-align: middle;">
            <img src="./s5_files/cog-2x(1).png" alt="Settings">
        </button>
    </div>
</div>
Settings offers all sorts of interesting options. Spend some time trying them all out. The Diagram Theme dropdown is a great way to change the look of a diagram quickly. Snippets are great too. And don't forget that Alt + Enter is a quick keystroke for refreshing your diagram.
<p></p>
<p>Happy diagramming!</p>
<br>

